  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Energy obligated $51.3B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy made 4,456 awards with an average award size of $11.5M, and obligations were up 5.6% year over year. Facilities Support Services accounted for the largest share of spending at $25.1B for the period, followed by multiple Research and Development categories that together represent a substantial portion of the portfolio. Top vendor concentrations are pronounced: TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC obligated $5.3B and NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC obligated $5.2B, with other national lab management and defense-related contractors in the top ten. Historical obligations show a multi-year increase from $37.7B in FY21 to $51.3B in FY26. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What are Energy's biggest spending categories?",
        "body": "Facilities Support Services is the largest category with $25.1B in obligations. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the next-largest single category at $8B, with other R&D subcategories and Remediation Services ranging from $3.5B down to $730M. The portfolio also includes $2.9B for Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing and $785M for Hazardous Waste Treatment and Disposal."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who captures the most contract dollars at Energy?",
        "body": "TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC is the top vendor with $5.3B in obligations, followed closely by NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC with $5.2B. LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC obligated $3.6B and SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC obligated $3.4B, with five additional vendors each receiving between $3.3B and $1.6B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Energy spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Energy obligated $51.3B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy made 4,456 awards with an average award size of $11.5M, and obligations were up 5.6% year over year. Historical totals show obligations of $37.7B in FY21, $41.2B in FY22, $44.6B in FY23, $46B in FY24, and $48.5B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Energy buy?",
      "a": "Energy buys a mix of Facilities Support Services and R&D work. Facilities Support Services totaled $25.1B, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences totaled $8B, and additional R&D subcategories, Remediation Services, and manufacturing and disposal services account for the remaining top categories."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Energy's largest contractors?",
      "a": "TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC is the largest contractor with $5.3B in obligations, followed by NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC with $5.2B. Other top contractors include LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $3.6B, SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC at $3.4B, and CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC at $3.3B."
